# Desktop ids (no .desktop suffix) removed from the omarchy launcher.hides
# list before it is written into the working prefix. Omarchy keeps hiding
# everything else, so a row upstream adds still lands; only a name listed
# here is put back in the launcher.
#
# Every row must still be in the omarchy list. A name upstream stops hiding
# makes this row a silent no-op, so monarchy_check_launcher_unhides fails
# rather than let it rot.
#
# libreoffice-fresh ships all six applications and omarchy shows three.
# Base additionally wants a java-runtime for its default HSQLDB engine.
libreoffice-base
libreoffice-draw
libreoffice-math
